    { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which ATEX zone applies in a hydrogen laboratory container?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "In normal operation with tight H₂ plant, Zone 2 typically applies – an explosive atmosphere occurs only rarely and briefly. Directly at vent lines or inside test chambers, Zone 1 can arise locally. Zoning is set out in the explosion protection document under BetrSichV §6, taking account of TRBS 2152 and DGUV Information 213-053." } },
