    { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many air changes does an H₂ laboratory need?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "DGUV Information 213-053 specifies for hydrogen laboratories an air-change rate of at least 8 h⁻¹ in standard ventilation. For trials with an elevated release risk or in an alarm case, this is raised to 15–25 h⁻¹. Extract must be taken at the highest point of the ceiling because H₂ is around 14× lighter than air." } },
    { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which standard applies to battery misuse tests?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "For industrial lithium cells IEC 62619 and IEC 62620, for stationary storage UL 9540A (thermal-runaway characterisation), for traction batteries ECE R100 and UN 38.3 (transport testing). For crash, nail and overcharge tests all standards require an enclosed test volume with defined ventilation and fire fighting – a container with a pressure-relief area meets this without an onerous special permit in the main building." } },
