    { "@type": "Question", "name": "Why a container rather than the main building for explosion-protected trials?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Safety distance: a free-standing container more easily meets the TRBS 2152 minimum distances to neighbouring buildings and traffic routes. Pressure relief: wall or roof areas can be executed as bursting panels. Permitting: the Ex zone remains spatially limited; the rest of the site is unaffected. Modular expansion: when the research grows, the next container goes beside it." } },
